<!doctype html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#010138" />
    <title>Bilateral stimulation</title>
    <link rel="icon" href="/favicon-32x32.png" />
  </head>
  <body>
    <main id="stage" aria-label="Bilateral stimulation">
      <p class="landscape-hint">For a wider view, rotate your phone to landscape.</p>
      <div id="track" class="track" aria-hidden="true">
        <div class="line"></div>
        <div id="ball" class="ball"></div>
      </div>
      <div class="session-controls">
        <div class="transport">
          <button id="start" class="run">Run</button>
          <button id="stop" hidden aria-label="Stop and reset">Stop</button>
        </div>
        <div id="duration-choice" class="duration-choice" role="group" aria-label="Next session length">
          <input id="duration" type="hidden" value="30" />
          <button data-duration="30" aria-pressed="true">30s</button>
          <button data-duration="45" aria-pressed="false">45s</button>
          <button data-duration="60" aria-pressed="false">1min</button>
          <button data-duration="90" aria-pressed="false">1min30</button>
          <button data-duration="120" aria-pressed="false">2min</button>
        </div>
        <p id="remaining" class="remaining" hidden></p>
      </div>
    </main>

    <div id="drawer-rail" class="drawer-rail">
      <button id="settings-toggle" class="settings-toggle" aria-label="Open settings" aria-controls="settings-panel" aria-expanded="false" title="Settings">
        <svg width="18" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 3v18M12 3v18M19 3v18"/><path d="M2 8h6M9 16h6M16 9h6" stroke-width="4"/></svg>
      </button>
      <aside id="settings-panel" class="settings-panel" aria-label="Session settings" inert>
        <div class="panel-heading"><h1>Settings</h1><button id="settings-close" class="icon-button" aria-label="Close settings">×</button></div>
        <p id="feedback" class="sr-only" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
        <div class="settings">
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Stimuli</legend>
            <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" id="visual" checked />Visual <span>Moving ball</span></label>
            <label class="choice"><input type="checkbox" id="audio" />Audio <span>Alternating tones</span></label>
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Visual & rhythm</legend>
            <div class="parameter-heading"><label class="range-label" for="speed">Tracking pace <output id="speed-value">0.50 cycles/s</output></label><button id="default-speed" class="default-button" aria-label="Default tracking pace">Default</button></div>
            <input type="range" id="speed" min="0.1" max="1.5" step="0.05" value="0.5" />
            <p class="helper" id="pace-detail">2 seconds for left → right → left.</p>
            <p class="helper">Pause to adjust. Choose a pace you can comfortably follow without strain. This sets round trips per second; a wider path means faster travel.</p>
            <div class="parameter-heading"><label class="range-label" for="width">Travel width <output id="width-value">100%</output></label><button id="default-width" class="default-button" aria-label="Default travel width">Default</button></div>
            <input id="width" type="range" min="50" max="100" value="100" step="5" />
          </fieldset>
          <fieldset>
            <legend>Audio</legend>
            <p class="helper"><strong>Muted wood</strong><br />A soft, low marimba recording with a natural decay.</p>
            <button id="preview-sound" class="preview-sound">Preview · left → right</button>
            <label class="range-label" for="volume">Tone volume <output id="volume-value">20%</output></label>
            <input type="range" id="volume" min="0" max="60" value="20" />
            <p class="helper">Start with your device volume low.</p>
            <details id="audio-guide"><summary>Headphone setup</summary>
              <ol><li>Use stereo headphones, with L on your left ear.</li><li>Choose them in your device’s sound output. Turn off mono audio, spatial audio, and head tracking.</li><li>Test each side below. The tone should play only in the named ear.</li></ol>
              <p class="helper">If both ears hear the same tone, check mono audio in your accessibility settings. This page cannot detect your physical audio routing.</p>
            </details>
            <div class="test-buttons"><button id="test-left">← Test left</button><button id="test-right">Test right →</button></div>
            <p id="audio-status" class="helper" role="status">Click Preview to listen.</p>
            <details><summary>No sound?</summary><p>Test and Run activate browser audio directly; no microphone permission is needed. Check that this tab is unmuted and your headphones are the selected system output.</p><p>In Chrome, open the controls beside the address bar → Site settings → Sound → Allow. If the embedded preview stays silent, open this same local URL in a regular Chrome tab and test there.</p><p>The tests play the same pulse as the session. Increase the volume gradually if needed. If sound still feels late over Bluetooth, try wired headphones; the browser may not report all wireless delay.</p></details>
          </fieldset>
        </div>
        <div class="panel-extras"><button id="fullscreen">Full screen ↗</button><p>Space: run / pause · Esc: stop<br />While paused, Restart begins a fresh set.</p></div>
        <details><summary>Before you begin</summary><p>This is a bilateral stimulus tool, not guided EMDR treatment. Trauma processing should be done with a trained therapist. For independent use, stay with your present surroundings rather than deliberately recalling distressing memories. Stop if you feel dizzy, overwhelmed, or disconnected.</p><p id="stage-hint">Sit comfortably. Let your eyes follow the ball.</p><p>Each set ends automatically. Take time to look around and check how you feel before choosing to continue.</p><a href="https://www.emdria.org/about-emdr-therapy/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">About EMDR therapy ↗</a></details>
        <details><summary>About the pace</summary><p>There is no universal clinically established speed for independent use. One laboratory study compared 0.8 and 1.2 full eye-movement cycles per second. These experimental settings are not a prescription for self-treatment.</p><p>The default of 0.5 cycles/s is an interface setting, not a therapeutic dose. One cycle means left → right → left; a tone plays at each endpoint. Use a comfortable pace or your clinician’s settings.</p><a href="https://www.frontiersin.org/journals/psychiatry/articles/10.3389/fpsyt.2015.00045/full" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Read the study ↗</a></details>
        <details><summary>Other stimuli, privacy & credits</summary><p>Alternating tactile taps and handheld vibrating devices are also used in EMDR. This tool provides visual and audio cues only.</p><p>Everything runs in your browser. No account or session recordings. Settings reset when you leave.</p><p>Instrument recordings: Sam Gossner & Simon Dalzell, VSCO 2 Community Edition (CC0). Edited for this tool. <a href="/audio/emdr/CREDITS.md" target="_blank">Sample credits</a>.</p></details>
      </aside>
    </div>
    <script>
      import '../scripts/emdr';
    </script>
  </body>
</html>

<style>
